        "# Extended Thinking\n\n## tabela of Conteúdo\n- [Configuração](#Configuração)\n- [Basic example](#basic-example)\n- [streaming com extended thinking](#streaming-com-extended-thinking)\n- [Token counting e context janela management](#token-counting-e-context-janela-management)\n- [Understanding redacted thinking](#understanding-redacted-thinking-blocks)\n- [Handling erro cases](#handling-erro-cases)\n\neste notebook demonstrates como para use Claude 3.7 Sonnet's extended thinking recurso com various Exemplos e edge cases.\n\nExtended thinking gives Claude 3.7 Sonnet enhanced reasoning capabilities para complexo tasks, enquanto also providing transparency into its step-by-step thought processo antes isso delivers its final answer. quando extended thinking is turned on, Claude creates `thinking` content blocks onde isso outputs its interno reasoning. Claude incorporates insights de este reasoning antes crafting a final resposta. Para mais informações on extended thinking, see our [Documentação](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/construir-com-claude/extended-thinking)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "python"
        }
      },
      "source": [
        "## Configuração\n\nprimeiro, let's instalar the necessary packages e definir up our environment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "python"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%pip install anthropic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "python"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "importar anthropic\n",
        "importar os\n",
        "\n",
        "# definir your api key as an environment variable or directly\n",
        "# os.environ[\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\"] = \"your-api-key-here\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initialize the client\n",
        "client = anthropic.Anthropic()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Helper functions\n",
        "def print_thinking_response(response):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Pretty imprimir a message response with thinking blocks.\"\"\"\n",
        "    imprimir(\"\\n==== FULL RESPONSE ====\")\n",
        "    para block in response.content:\n",
        "        se block.tipo == \"thinking\":\n",
        "            imprimir(\"\\n🧠 THINKING BLOCK:\")\n",
        "            # Show truncated thinking para readability\n",
        "            imprimir(block.thinking[:500] + \"...\" se len(block.thinking) > 500 senão block.thinking)\n",
        "            imprimir(f\"\\n[Signature available: {bool(getattr(block, 'signature', None))}]\")\n",
        "            se hasattr(block, 'signature') and block.signature:\n",
        "                imprimir(f\"[Signature (first 50 chars): {block.signature[:50]}...]\")\n",
        "        elif block.tipo == \"redacted_thinking\":\n",
        "            imprimir(\"\\n🔒 REDACTED THINKING BLOCK:\")\n",
        "            imprimir(f\"[Data length: {len(block.data) se hasattr(block, 'data') senão 'N/A'}]\")\n",
        "        elif block.tipo == \"text\":\n",
        "            imprimir(\"\\n✓ FINAL ANSWER:\")\n",
        "            imprimir(block.text)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    imprimir(\"\\n==== END RESPONSE ====\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def count_tokens(messages):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Count tokens para a given message list.\"\"\"\n",
        "    result = client.messages.count_tokens(\n",
        "        model=\"claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219\",\n",
        "        messages=messages\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    retornar result.input_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Basic example\n\nLet's iniciar com a basic example para show extended thinking in action:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "python"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "nome": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "\n",
            "==== FULL RESPONSE ====\n",
            "\n",
            "🧠 THINKING BLOCK:\n",
            "let's work through this problem step by step:\n",
            "\n",
            "Initial situation:\n",
            "- Three people each pay $10, para a total of $30 given to the manager.\n",
            "- The room actually costs $25.\n",
            "- Manager gives $5 to the bellboy to retornar to the customers.\n",
            "- Bellboy keeps $2 and gives $1 back to each person ($3 total).\n",
            "\n",
            "After these transactions:\n",
            "- Each person has effectively paid $9 (they paid $10 and got $1 back).\n",
            "- So the three people together paid $27.\n",
            "- The hotel kept $25 para the room.\n",
            "- The bellboy kept $2.\n",
            "\n",
            "So the mo...\n",
            "\n",
            "[Signature available: verdadeiro]\n",
            "[Signature (first 50 chars): EuYBCkQYAiJAGF6X7aWRuRByTdymAUdNOMC++3ZqSJv7jcY5Ly...]\n",
            "\n",
            "✓ FINAL ANSWER:\n",
            "# Hotel Bill Puzzle Solution\n",
            "\n",
            "This is a classic misdirection puzzle that confuses us by mixing up two different accounting approaches.\n",
            "\n",
            "## The actual flow of money\n",
            "\n",
            "1. Three people each pay $10, totaling $30\n",
            "2. The hotel keeps $25 para the room\n",
            "3. The bellboy keeps $2\n",
            "4. The guests receive $3 back ($1 each)\n",
            "\n",
            "## The accounting Erro in the puzzle\n",
            "\n",
            "The Erro occurs when the puzzle tries to add:\n",
            "- What the guests paid ($27 total after refunds)\n",
            "- What the bellboy kept ($2)\n",
            "\n",
            "This is incorrect accounting because the $2 the bellboy kept is already included in the $27 the guests paid. The money should be tracked from a single perspective.\n",
            "\n",
            "## Correct accounting\n",
            "\n",
            "From the guests' perspective:\n",
            "- $27 (what they ultimately paid)\n",
            "- = $25 (to the hotel) + $2 (to the bellboy)\n",
            "\n",
            "There is no missing dollar. The puzzle creates confusion by inappropriately adding money from different accounting perspectives.\n",
            "\n",
            "==== END RESPONSE ====\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def basic_thinking_example():\n",
        "    response = client.messages.create(\n",
        "        model=\"claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219\",\n",
        "        max_tokens=4000,\n",
        "        thinking= {\n",
        "            \"tipo\": \"enabled\",\n",
        "            \"budget_tokens\": 2000\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        messages=[{\n",
        "            \"role\": \"user\",\n",
        "            \"content\": \"Solve this puzzle: Three people check into a hotel. They pay $30 to the manager. The manager finds out that the room only costs $25 so he gives $5 to the bellboy to retornar to the three people. The bellboy, however, decides to keep $2 and gives $1 back to each person. Now, each person paid $10 and got back $1, so they paid $9 each, totaling $27. The bellboy kept $2, which makes $29. Where is the missing $1?\"\n",
        "        }]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    print_thinking_response(response)\n",
        "\n",
        "basic_thinking_example()"
      ]
    },
