      "source": [
        "## streaming com extended thinking\n\nEste exemplo shows como para handle streaming com thinking:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": nulo,
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "python"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "nome": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "\n",
            "--- Starting thinking block ---\n",
            "This is a classic mathematical puzzle that contains a misdirection in how the calculations are presented. let's parar isso down step by step:\n",
            "\n",
            "Initial situation:\n",
            "- Three people each pay $10, para a total of $30 given to the manager.\n",
            "- The room actually costs $25.\n",
            "- The manager gives $5 to the bellboy to retornar to the customers.\n",
            "- The bellboy keeps $2 and Retorna $1 to each person (total of $3 returned).\n",
            "\n",
            "Now, let's analyze the accounting:\n",
            "\n",
            "What actually happened:\n",
            "- The three people originally paid $30.\n",
            "- They got back $3 in total ($1 each).\n",
            "- So they actually paid $30 - $3 = $27 in total.\n",
            "- Of this $27, $25 went to the hotel para the room.\n",
            "- The remaining $2 went to the bellboy.\n",
            "- $25 + $2 = $27, which matches what the guests paid. Everything balances.\n",
            "\n",
            "The Erro in the puzzle is in how isso frames the question. The puzzle states \"each person paid $10 and got back $1, so they paid $9 each, totaling $27. The bellboy kept $2, which makes $29.\" This is mixing up different accounting Métodos. \n",
            "\n",
            "The $27 that the guests paid in total should be divided as:\n",
            "- $25 para the room\n",
            "- $2 para the bellboy\n",
            "\n",
            "When we add the bellboy's $2 to the guests' $27, we're double-counting the $2, which creates the illusion of a missing dollar. The $2 is already included in the $27, so we shouldn't add isso again.\n",
            "\n",
            "Another way to think about isso: Out of the original $30, $25 went to the hotel, $3 went back to the guests, and $2 went to the bellboy. That's $25 + $3 + $2 = $30, so everything is accounted para.\n",
            "[Completed thinking block, 1492 characters]\n",
            "--- Finished thinking block ---\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "--- Starting text block ---\n",
            "# The Missing $1 Puzzle Solution\n",
            "\n",
            "This puzzle uses a misleading way of accounting that creates confusion. let's clarify what actually happened:\n",
            "\n",
            "## The correct accounting:\n",
            "- Three people paid $30 total initially\n",
            "- The room cost $25\n",
            "- The bellboy kept $2\n",
            "- The guests received $3 back ($1 each)\n",
            "\n",
            "So where did all the money go?\n",
            "- $25 went to the hotel\n",
            "- $2 went to the bellboy\n",
            "- $3 went back to the guests\n",
            "- $25 + $2 + $3 = $30 ✓\n",
            "\n",
            "## The Erro in the puzzle:\n",
            "The puzzle incorrectly adds the $27 paid by the guests (after refunds) to the $2 kept by the bellboy. This is a mistake because the $2 kept by the bellboy is already part of the $27.\n",
            "\n",
            "The puzzle creates the illusion of a missing dollar by mixing two different perspectives:\n",
            "1. How much the guests paid ($27 total)\n",
            "2. Where the original $30 went (hotel + bellboy + refunds)\n",
            "\n",
            "There is no missing dollar - isso's just an accounting trick!--- Finished text block ---\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "--- Message Completo ---\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def streaming_with_thinking():\n",
        "    with client.messages.stream(\n",
        "        model=\"claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219\",\n",
        "        max_tokens=4000,\n",
        "        thinking={\n",
        "            \"tipo\": \"enabled\",\n",
        "            \"budget_tokens\": 2000\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        messages=[{\n",
        "            \"role\": \"user\",\n",
        "            \"content\": \"Solve this puzzle: Three people check into a hotel. They pay $30 to the manager. The manager finds out that the room only costs $25 so he gives $5 to the bellboy to retornar to the three people. The bellboy, however, decides to keep $2 and gives $1 back to each person. Now, each person paid $10 and got back $1, so they paid $9 each, totaling $27. The bellboy kept $2, which makes $29. Where is the missing $1?\"\n",
        "        }]\n",
        "    ) as stream:\n",
        "        # Track what we're currently building\n",
        "        current_block_type = None\n",
        "        current_content = \"\"\n",
        "        \n",
        "        para event in stream:\n",
        "            se event.tipo == \"content_block_start\":\n",
        "                current_block_type = event.content_block.tipo\n",
        "                imprimir(f\"\\n--- Starting {current_block_type} block ---\")\n",
        "                current_content = \"\"\n",
        "                \n",
        "            elif event.tipo == \"content_block_delta\":\n",
        "                se event.delta.tipo == \"thinking_delta\":\n",
        "                    imprimir(event.delta.thinking, end=\"\", flush=verdadeiro)  # Just imprimir dots para thinking to avoid clutter\n",
        "                    current_content += event.delta.thinking\n",
        "                elif event.delta.tipo == \"text_delta\":\n",
        "                    imprimir(event.delta.text, end=\"\", flush=verdadeiro)\n",
        "                    current_content += event.delta.text\n",
        "                    \n",
        "            elif event.tipo == \"content_block_stop\":\n",
        "                se current_block_type == \"thinking\":\n",
        "                    # Just show a summary para thinking\n",
        "                    imprimir(f\"\\n[Completed thinking block, {len(current_content)} characters]\")\n",
        "                elif current_block_type == \"redacted_thinking\":\n",
        "                    imprimir(\"\\n[Redacted thinking block]\")\n",
        "                imprimir(f\"--- Finished {current_block_type} block ---\\n\")\n",
        "                current_block_type = None\n",
        "                \n",
        "            elif event.tipo == \"message_stop\":\n",
        "                imprimir(\"\\n--- Message Completo ---\")\n",
        "\n",
        "streaming_with_thinking()"
      ]
    },
